ven  remembering her own name but regardless  just a few weeks later she went back to  filming and to add on to that the doctor  told her that there was a second growth  on her brain that could pop at any time  emilia said it was crazy intense we were  in the desert in a quarry in like 90  degree heat and i had the consistent  fear that i was going to have another  brain hemorrhage i spent a lot of time  just being like am i going to die is  that going to happen on set because that  would be really inconvenient  she was also heavily fatigued during  this period and even needed an air  conditioning car on set so the fact that  emilia was able to endure all of this  while delivering reams of dothraki and  blistering heat is crazily impressive  and i admire her so much  for a few small stories that i'll bang  out quickly the king's landing set for  the iron throne room was ironically  really cold and one of the handmade  actors wearing a toga pass out from  being so cold which is ironic given that  king's landing is supposed to be pretty  warm then in season 3 during the scene  where jaime lannister is in the mud  getting beaten up by lock nikolaj coster  waldo had one of his ribs broken nikolaj  though wasn't that upset about it  because it was an honest mistake and it  was just a misjudged kick  then there's also the time where david  and dan put a baby on a real block of  freezing ice when asked why they  couldn't have just used fake ice they  said fake ice and close up just never  looks real despite them barely putting  any emphasis on the ice since it was  briefly shown in like two shots then as  you know in the scene the night king has  to interact with the baby and touch him  thus making the baby scream on set and  david and dan realized they were  traumatizing the baby after that david  and damn rudely insisted on seeing the  baby's penis to prove that the baby was  a boy which was both really weird and  made the mother uncomfortable i don't  know why david and dan would want that  so much when it was told to us the scene  prior that the baby was a boy so you  don't need to show his privates moving  over to the battle of the bastards liam  cunningham who plays davos seaworth  almost got decapitated by a russian  crane arm while he was on his horse he  says the horse wanted to play with its  mates and ride off he jumped two feet to  the left and the camera went straight  over where my head was i could have been  decapitated but i ducked the crew were  horrified but luckily he wasn't injured  there was really no one at fault in the  situation since horses can be  unpredictable since we're on season six  sophie turner who plays sansa stark was  told not to wash her hair for long  filming periods since she's supposed to  look dirtier given that she doesn't have  access to a castle she said it is the  most amazing feeling to have a shower  after you go a week and you have snow  and mud and horseshits and all these  disgusting things in your hair to me it  seems like overkill to force your actor  into bad hygiene when you can easily  fake that with makeup and wigs but  sophie turner didn't seem that upset  about the situation moving on though  since that isn't too crazy during the  scene where lancel lannister chases a  kid into the catacombs during the trial  of the seven eugene michael simon who  plays lancel was forced to crawl through  batshits and start bats down there also  keep in mind that his spinal cord was  severed so he was only allowed to crawl  with his arms and upper body for the  entire duration of filming by the end i  was so exhausted and i was literally  frothing at the mouth and the ground was  covered in blood [ __ ] sweat and a few  tears that doesn't seem too bad but  there's an additional thing that happens  that pushes this occurrence over the  edge a bit they put petroleum on top of  the wildfire when the fire went off it  burned off my eyebrows and i could smell  my own burnt hair i just feel bad for  the poor guy since this was probably his  final scene along with hannah who plays  septo nella moving on to something  bigger for the action set piece where  euron greyjoy ambushes yara and theon's  fleet the entire sequence was filmed  pretty chaotically it's detailed that  the ship was on a rig with big water  cannon shooting massive swaths of water  at the actors on top of fire getting  shot out as well obara's stunt double  even had her wig caught on fire and to  add on to all of this the floor was made  out of unstable balsa wood jessica  henwick who plays one of the sand snakes  said at least three crew members fell  through the floor because some of it was  balsa wood so you could smash through it  but it wasn't marked off so occasionally  you would just hear a yelp as another  crew member fell through which to me is  pretty wild and seems like some kind of  safety violation so with all that in  mind the actors were also required to  fight viscerally and were even  criticized for not having enough energy  gemma wellin who played yara greyjoy was  hospitalized during the fight sequence  although there aren't any details as to  why she was hospitalized it could really  have been a number of things at this  rates also in this sequence jessica  henwick gets choked to death with a whip  for her death scene and it did not go  smoothly according to her she said there  was an accident where pillow almost  freaking choked me out with my own whip  then they were shoving me onto a  forklift and hoisting me up there they  wanted to tie me there and put pressure  around my neck as soon as they put me on  it i was like get it off get it off get  it off so yeah that entire sequence did  not go very well  while filming beyond the wall rory  mccann who plays sandra clegane had to  carry a real person on his shoulders  that played a captive white and at one  point he fell down and hurt his leg rory  says i had this guy on my shoulder for  days and days it didn't work with a  