r  lost its initial director just a few  weeks before filming and kit harrington  having to film scenes in season 3 with a  broken ankle but to cap off this video  david and dan were notorious for  carrying out some big pranks on their  cast members primarily in the form of  fake scripts there are quite a few of  these instances but two stand out to me  that i want to mention one of these  occurrences happened to kit harrington  in season 1 where he fights a white for  the first time to save dior mormonts  david and dan wrote the scene where  instead of jon burning his hand when  picking up the torch he instead catches  his hair on fire and it all burns away  leaving a bald jon snow with major  scarring all over his face weiss told  kid harrington that hbo were worried  that jon snow's storyline was too harry  potter and they wanted to do something  to make it darker the messed up thing to  me is that david and dan ran with this  joke all the way up until filming the  scene making it to where they made kit  believe he would be playing a disfigured  character for the rest of the show and  he would be bound to a makeup chair for  many hours  luckily though kit was a good sport  about it but the same couldn't be said  about liam cunningham who plays davos  for this instance david benioff wanted  davos to have a crush on missandei when  they first met and liam was not happy  liam said i fought them i'm not effing  doing it it's the only thing i ever  stood up to them on the woman is a  goddess but with davos's history with  leona mormont and shireen you can't have  him getting the hots for a young woman  he then went on to say he wasn't 100  sure if david and dan were actually  kidding and i love that he was genuinely  uncertain about that fact kind of  alluding to their incompetence at  writing but if they were being serious  then that would have been atrocious so  thank god liam stood up to them on that  issue liam further says you're not  undoing my hard work engendering the  sympathy of the audience to have him be  a perv so from this air of doubt  established between fake script pranks  and actors genuinely not being sure if  the scripts were real most actors  thought the season 8 scripts were fake  since these stories are a bit more  popular i'll run through a few quickly  for isaac hempstead wright who plays  bran he legitimately thought it was a  joke that he became the king and maisie  williams initially disagreed with her  character getting the final blow on the  night king along with those facts the  season 8 scripts essentially gave emilia  clarke an existential crisis because the  characters she idolized suddenly turned  into a villain which even she didn't see  coming emilia said i cried when they  read the scripts it was an effing  struggle i left the house and took my  keys and phone and walked back with  blisters on my feet because i walked for  hours conwath hill plays varys also  famously did not like the season 8  scripts he says at the time nothing  could console me i kept thinking what  did i do wrong you couldn't help the  feeling that you failed in some way that  you hadn't lived up to the expectation  that you didn't know about  he also admitted after this that he was  okay now but he did say that his  character dropped off a bit in terms of  quality overall these are the main  findings i've found through the book  fire cannot kill a dragon and other  sources and there are other minor  problems that i skipped over that i  don't think are really worth featuring  thank you for watching and if you're at  all interested in the making of game of  thrones then check out fire cannot kill  a dragon

