ring the  sympathy of the audience to have him be  a perv so from this air of doubt  established between fake script pranks  and actors genuinely not being sure if  the scripts were real most actors  thought the season 8 scripts were fake  since these stories are a bit more  popular i'll run through a few quickly  for isaac hempstead wright who plays  bran he legitimately thought it was a  joke that he became the king and maisie  williams initially disagreed with her  character getting the final blow on the  night king along with those facts the  season 8 scripts essentially gave emilia  clarke an existential crisis because the  characters she idolized suddenly turned  into a villain which even she didn't see  coming emilia said i cried when they  read the scripts it was an effing  struggle i left the house and took my  keys and phone and walked back with  blisters on my feet because i walked for  hours conwath hill plays varys also  famously did not like the season 8  scripts he says at the time nothing  could console me i kept thinking what  did i do wrong you couldn't help the  feeling that you failed in some way that  you hadn't lived up to the expectation  that you didn't know about  he also admitted after this that he was  okay now but he did say that his  character dropped off a bit in terms of  quality overall these are the main  findings i've found through the book  fire cannot kill a dragon and other  sources and there are other minor  problems that i skipped over that i  don't think are really worth featuring  thank you for watching and if you're at  all interested in the making of game of  thrones then check out fire cannot kill  a dragon
 

